// GuardTalkLauncherOverlay — F-HOME-LAYOUT (FR-E)
// Static RRO overriding com.android.launcher3 default_workspace_*.xml for ALL
// 9 grids (2x2, 3x3, 4x4, 4x5, 5x5, 5x8, 6x5, 7x3, 8x3). The active grid for
// tokay/Pixel 9 is 5_by_5 (per device_profiles.xml grid-option "5_by_5",
// deviceCategory="phone|multi_display", minWidth 406dp) but ALL grids are
// overridden so the GuardTalk layout wins regardless of which grid Launcher3
// selects at runtime.
//
// Layout-only override: ships only GuardTalk app icon(s) on the default
// home + hotseat. No app install/uninstall is performed here; excised
// apps remain available in the all-apps drawer if still installed.
//
// PARTITION MATCH (T-HOME-ROOTCAUSE): Launcher3 is system_ext_specific
// (packages/apps/Launcher3/Android.bp). On Android 14+ (SDK 34+), OverlayManager
// filters out static RROs whose target is in a DIFFERENT partition than the
// overlay itself. A product-specific overlay targeting a system_ext app is
// silently ignored at boot. This overlay MUST be system_ext_specific so it
// lands in /system_ext/overlay/ alongside its target.
// CERTIFICATE FIX (T-HOME-ROOTCAUSE): Launcher3 ships with NO `certificate:`
// field, so Soong signs it with the platform key (the AOSP default for
// privileged system apps). On Android 12+ (SDK 31+), OverlayManager applies a
// static RRO that overrides NON-overlayable resources ONLY when the overlay is
// signed with the SAME certificate as its target package. `default_workspace_*`
// is NOT declared `<overlayable>` in Launcher3, so a test-key static RRO is
// silently dropped at boot — the home layout never changes, even after a clean
// userdata wipe. Signing the overlay with "platform" matches Launcher3's cert
// so OverlayManager enables it and the GuardTalk workspace wins on first boot.
runtime_resource_overlay {
    name: "GuardTalkLauncherOverlay",
    sdk_version: "current",
    system_ext_specific: true,
    certificate: "platform",
}
